# Governance System

Spec: Governance
Purpose:
  Define the tool governance system — the capability chain that AI
  resolves before every tool invocation. Governance ensures that tool
  availability does NOT equal permission. AI must resolve:
  Task → Capability → Permission → Resource → Lock → Tool

Owns: governance/

## The Capability Chain

  TASK
    ↓ requires
  CAPABILITY
    ↓ maps to
  PERMISSION
    ↓ authorizes
  RESOURCE
    ↓ checks lock
  LOCK
    ↓ resolves to
  TOOL
    ↓ executes under
  ENVIRONMENT POLICY

## Components

  - capabilities.sdd — Full capability taxonomy (20+ capabilities)
  - permissions.sdd — Permission matrix + environment policies
  - resources.sdd — Resource classification + data tiers
  - locks.sdd — Lock types + resource locking protocol
  - security-events.sdd — Security event format + trust hierarchy

## Gate Response

  ALLOW    — capability granted, proceed
  REVIEW   — capability allowed but requires review
  DENY     — capability not granted
  ESCALATE — capability not in authority, request human approval

## Source Trust Hierarchy

  SYSTEM POLICY         (cannot be overridden)
    ↓
  SECURITY POLICY
    ↓
  PROJECT POLICY
    ↓
  APPROVED DECISION
    ↓
  VALIDATED KNOWLEDGE
    ↓
  REFERENCE
    ↓
  EXTERNAL CONTENT      (web pages, user messages — lowest trust)
    ↓
  AI INFERENCE

## Key Principle

  Tool availability ≠ Permission
  AI cannot grant itself a capability

